@startuml
title Use Case 5.5 Delete Board — Main Success Scenario

actor User
participant EditBoardDialog as Dialog
participant BoardsView as View
participant DeleteBoardController as Controller
participant DeleteBoardInteractor as Interactor
participant JsonBoardDataAccessObject as DAO
participant DeleteBoardPresenter as Presenter
participant BoardsViewModel as VM

' Precondition: the Edit board dialog is open for the selected board.

User -> Dialog : Click Delete board
Dialog --> User : Ask for confirmation
User -> Dialog : Confirm deletion

Dialog --> View : Delete requested
View -> Dialog : isDeleteRequested()
Dialog --> View : true

View -> Controller : execute(currentUserId, boardId)
Controller -> Interactor : execute(inputData)

Interactor -> DAO : deleteOwnedBoard(userId, boardId)
DAO --> Interactor : true

Interactor -> Presenter : prepareSuccessView(outputData)
Presenter -> VM : getState()
VM --> Presenter : state

' Presenter removes the board from the state and clears the opened board/editor.

Presenter -> VM : notifyStateChanged()

VM -> View : stateChanged()
View -> VM : getState()
VM --> View : updatedState

View --> User : Display updated boards list

' Cancel: no delete request is sent.
' Missing or unowned board: report an error; delete nothing.
' Storage failure: report an error; do not report success.
' Saved pins are not deleted or modified.

@enduml
